HALL REPORT  \nITS FINDINGS TO THE PRESIDENT\nBy virtue of the authority vested in \nme by section 10 of the Railway Labor \nAct, as amended (45 U.S.C. 160), and as \nPresident of the United States, I hereby \nextend until June 20, 1961, the time \nwithin which the emergency board cre­\nated by Executive Order No. 10919 of \nFebruary 17, 1961, to investigate a dis­\npute between Pan American World \nAirways, Inc., and certain of its em­\nployees, represented by the Flight En­\ngineers’  International Association, PAA \nChapter, a labor organization, shall re­\nport its findings to the President.\nJ ohn F. K ennedy\nT he W hite  H ouse ,\nMarch 18,1961.","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-10926-9e57245c6e.txt","sha256":"c4233561cbec0e9468f33001657790d5d401b6cbd6f2e268b2d138bcbd9d6c2b","source":{"line":1972,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"6c8e5178bfef1bb27cb0627e20666ec4378044609722bb47a415510912b8e45d"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:10926\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1961-03-21/pdf/FR-1961-03-21.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 9e57245c6e3141acd9b2ae498cb39500146348a1fa63abbb3d4fbfd2ea8113b7\nLocation: 26 FR 2331, PDF pages 3-3 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 3 of 56 ===\nPresidential Documents\nTitle 3— THE PRESIDENT\nExecutive Order 10926\nAMENDING EXECUTIVE ORDER NO.  \n10919,1  FEBRUARY 17, 1961, TO  \nEXTEND THE TIME WITHIN WHICH  \nTHE BOARD CREATED THEREIN,  \nTO INVESTIGATE A DISPUTE BE­\nTWEEN PAN AMERICAN WORLD  \nAIRWAYS, INC., AND CERTAIN OF  \nITS EMPLOYEES, SHALL REPORT  \nITS FINDINGS TO THE PRESIDENT\nBy virtue of the authority vested in \nme by section 10 of the Railway Labor \nAct, as amended (45 U.S.C. 160), and as \nPresident of the United States, I hereby \nextend until June 20, 1961, the time \nwithin which the emergency board cre­\nated by Executive Order No. 10919 of \nFebruary 17, 1961, to investigate a dis­\npute between Pan American World \nAirways, Inc., and certain of its em­\nployees, represented by the Flight En­\ngineers’  International Association, PAA \nChapter, a labor organization, shall re­\nport its findings to the President.\nJ ohn F. K ennedy\nT he W hite  H ouse ,\nMarch 18,1961.\n{F.R. Doc. 61-2525; Filed, Mar. 20. 1961;\n10:24 a.m.]\n126 F.R. 1","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_10926.txt","sha256":"638a6a29ea554292b91398ec7964e77dab398419bf3777f1d5ea8f8af7e66645","source":{"line":982,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"ddaca370c0f1db66e245c9d51234a22d989546158f9a13b61dd0badeff640d02"}}]}
